 3. 🏦 What Wall Street is watching 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios. Photo: Spencer Platt/Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Investors are closely watching elections in states with major data center projects planned, down to the makeup of local utility commission boards.

 🎰 Why it matters: New restrictions could delay major projects and rattle the AI trade that's driving the stock market and helping power the U.S. economy, Axios Markets co-author Emily Peck reports. 📊 Stunning stat: The outcomes of 10 governors' races could affect 67.4 gigawatts of planned data center capacity — $2.5 trillion worth (!) — more than is currently operating in the U.S., according to research firm Cleanview.

 A Democratic sweep would be the most negative outcome for AI investor sentiment, Morgan Stanley projects. Keep reading ... Get Axios Business Suite . 

 
 
