 How Amazon is creating jobs and investing in data center communities 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 We've codified our practices into the Amazon Data Center Commitment: investing in energy and water infrastructure, creating skilled local jobs, engaging openly and contributing over $1 billion over the next five years to the communities where we invest through our new Built Together program. 


 
 &nbsp; 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 4. 📍 Mapped: AI&#x27;s $10 trillion buildout 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Data Center Map . Map: Erin Davis/Axios Despite more than 300 local moratoriums, U.S. data center development is moving at a blistering pace, Axios' Bradley Olson and Erin Davis report. 

 🚧 But political, regulatory, supply and environmental hurdles are delaying some major projects. Case in point: In New Mexico, Oracle recently took steps to protect itself from steep costs tied to delays of the $165 billion Project Jupiter stemming from local opposition, permitting roadblocks and power supply challenges.

 Data: Michael Bommarito, 2026, Survey of Data Center Moratoria . Chart: Erin Davis/Axios The bottom line: Growing opposition is slowing some projects but hasn't forced the buildout to stop. 

