 &nbsp; 
 
 
 7. 📺 The new attack line 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios. Stock: Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Campaigns and outside groups have spent $173 million on almost entirely negative ads about data centers during this year's general election, Axios' Holly Otterbein and Alex Thompson report from AdImpact data. 

 Over half of the total spending — about $95 million — is in four Rust Belt states: Ohio, Michigan, Wisconsin and Pennsylvania. 🔵 Democrats are driving the attacks, outspending Republicans $140 million to $28 million overall. 

 When Axios asked AdImpact if it could identify a single ad making an overtly positive case for data centers, it could not. 🎯 What to watch: The geography of today's backlash could offer an early glimpse of how AI could shape the political battlegrounds in 2028.

