 8. 🏘️ Sign of the times: Data Center Alley 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A housing development near data centers in Sterling, Va. Photo: Stephen Voss D.C. photographer Stephen Voss is trying to show how data centers actually affect the people living near them, Axios D.C. co-author Mimi Montgomery writes. 

 His project , " Dark Fiber ," documents how data center development has transformed Northern Virginia communities. A home near a data center in Gainesville, Va. Photo: Stephen Voss The data center boom is reshaping the D.C.-Virginia-Maryland region so quickly that some of the places Voss photographed just a few years ago already look different. 

